2186355882 1113 #uuid "113d15a6-0fe2-5e15-8f69-833b952efa0b" 13194139535576 true] [17592186355882 1145 "The norm of a vector $f(t)$ with respect to an inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ is defined as\n\n$$\n‖f(t)‖=\\sqrt{⟨f(t),f(t)⟩}.\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(t),f(t)⟩ & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(f(t))^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\,{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\,({cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(t-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t}{2}){|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =(\\pi -\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\pi }{2})-(0-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡0}{2}) \\\\  & =\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we made use of the trigonometric identities\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t=1\\,\\text{and}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\n$$\n\nFinally then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖f(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535576 true] [17592186355883 1000 #edb/ref 17592186355884 13194139535576 true] [17592186355883 1000 #edb/ref 17592186355885 13194139535576 true] [17592186355883 1000 #edb/ref 17592186355886 13194139535576 true] [17592186355883 1000 #edb/ref 17592186355887 13194139535576 true] [17592186355883 1000 #edb/ref 17592186355888 13194139535576 true] [17592186355883 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535576 true] [17592186355883 1041 "selection" 13194139535576 true] [17592186355883 1104 #edb/ref 17592186355886 13194139535576 true] [17592186355883 1110 #uuid "f92c7057-0bf9-564b-9a29-12f0bd5ccd63" 13194139535576 true] [17592186355884 1034 "\\sqrt{\\pi +1}" 13194139535576 true] [17592186355884 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535576 true] [17592186355884 1111 #uuid "8cff18d2-32c2-59a1-8da7-62f352c12793" 13194139535576 true] [17592186355885 1034 "\\sqrt{\\frac{\\pi }{2}}" 1319